name>ECHIGO MITSUAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OSAKA GAS CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI MINORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ECHIGO, MITSUAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OSAKA GAS CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, MINORU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ECHIGO MITSUAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI MINORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ECHIGO, MITSUAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, MINORU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for removing carbon monoxide which is contained in an amount of 1,000 ppm to a few percentages in a gas to be treated being rich in hydrogen, such as the reformed gas obtained by reforming a fuel such as natural gas or methanol, which method, using a system comprising two CO-removing units, comprises a first step removing carbon monoxide by methanation in the presence of a catalyst in a first CO-remover and a second step removing residual carbon monoxide by a catalytic oxidation reaction with the use of an oxidizing agent in a second CO-remover.  This method allows removing carbon monoxide very effectively, for example, to a level of tens of ppm or less (in some cases, 10 ppm) with a reduced loss of hydrogen even when carbon dioxide and methane are present.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de suppression du monoxyde de carbone contenu à raison de 1 000 ppm ou moins dans un gaz à traiter riche en hydrogène, tel que le gaz réformé obtenu par reformage d'un combustible, comme le gaz naturel ou le méthanol. Ledit procédé consiste d'abord, au moyen d'un système comportant deux unités de suppression du CO, à supprimer le monoxyde de carbone par méthanisation en présence d'un catalyseur dans une première unité de suppression du CO, puis à supprimer le monoxyde de carbone résiduel par une réaction d'oxydation catalytique au moyen d'un agent d'oxydation dans une deuxième unité de suppression de CO. Ledit procédé permet également la suppression très efficace du monoxyde de carbone, par exemple, jusqu'à un niveau de dizaines de ppm ou moins (dans certains cas 10 ppm) avec une perte d'hydrogène réduite, même lorsque du dioxyde de carbone et du méthane sont présents.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of 